From 71bb8f2841bafc3605ef56227b2da1e03e7ce9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yourself <user@shredder.lan>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:56:58 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] winehaiku.drv: rebase the Haiku graphics driver onto 11.8

The driver last built against Wine 7.8.  Since then the graphics drivers
were split into a PE half and a unix half, so this reinstates it under
the current conventions:

  - Makefile.in uses SOURCES/UNIXLIB/UNIX_LIBS instead of C_SRCS/RC_SRCS.
  - dllmain.c is the PE entry point and calls __wine_init_unix_call().
  - unixlib.h declares the PE -> unix call interface.

The BeAPI is C++-only but Wine`s internal headers are not C++-safe
(ntuser.h uses `class` and `virtual` as identifiers), so the driver is C
plus C++ with a plain-C seam declared in haikudrv_be.h -- the same shape
winemac.drv uses for its C / Objective-C split.  The C++ half is named
be_window.cpp rather than window.cpp because window.c and window.cpp
would both compile to window.o.

Several APIs the old driver used are gone in 11.x: __wine_send_input is
now NtUserSendHardwareInput, and IsWindowEnabled, PostMessageW,
SetWindowPos and GetClassLongW are reached through their NtUser
equivalents.  CreateThread is not available to unix-side code, so the
BApplication and per-window loops use spawn_thread.

ime.c and vulkan.cpp are left in the tree but out of SOURCES; they have
not been rebased yet.
